ACME ENTERPRISE - HYBRID WORK AND TRAVEL EXPENSE POLICY (REV-2026)

SEC-EXP-01: CLIENT-FACING TRAVEL REIMBURSEMENT
1. FLIGHT TICKET BOOKINGS
Employees traveling for verified business development meetings are allowed to book economy class tickets for domestic flights under 4 hours in duration. For cross-continental or international flights exceeding 7 consecutive hours, employees are pre-approved to book Premium Economy. Business Class bookings are strictly prohibited without written approval from the Chief Financial Officer (CFO).

2. DAILY MEAL ALLOWANCE (PER DIEM)
The daily maximum allowance for meals during active business travel is fixed at USD 85 per day within the United States, and USD 110 per day for international destinations. Alcohol purchases are completely non-reimbursable under any circumstances and must be split onto a personal payment card at the venue.

SEC-EXP-02: HOME OFFICE EQUIPMENT ALLOWANCES
1. RECURRING INTERNET SUBSIDIES
Permanent remote and hybrid employees can claim a recurring monthly stipend of USD 45 to offset the cost of home high-speed broadband internet. To receive this credit, employees must upload a copy of their monthly internet statement into the Expenseify system before the 5th day of the subsequent month.

2. HARDWARE AND ACCESSORIES BYPASSED
Laptops, external monitors, and corporate mobile phones are issued directly by IT Operations. Docking stations, keyboards, and mouse accessories purchased independently by employees are non-reimbursable unless ordered through the internal corporate hardware catalogue portal.
